  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A point source of light <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>, placed at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> infront of the centre of a plane mirror of width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, hangs vertically on a wall. A man walks infront of the mirror along a line parallel to the mirror at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;from it (see in the figure). The distance between the extreme points where he can see the image of the light source in the mirror is__<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ef11d240-f90b-4964-b644-0fe2b8e11f91-image.png\" style=\"width: 269px; height: 143px;\" /></p>",
